    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2X5GbEkTg1acJJLTffK42Xc)_\n\nFollows #193. In `sp-author-notes`:\n- `pub-author` values with quoted names (`\"A\", \"B\"`, `\"A\" \"B\"`, or a stray `\"Tim Wildschut`) give one author, and one `:person:` note, per name. A comma inside quotes (`\"Lee, Ann\"`) is still flipped.\n- `[[denote:ID][Name]]` links become `[[id:...]]` links when a note with that Denote identifier (`#+identifier:` or the file name) and an `:ID:` exists; otherwise they are reported and left alone. The preview lists them.\n- Unquoted names are split as before (`;` or `and`, never a comma). Links mixed with loose words are still left alone.\n\nTested: 13 ERT tests in Emacs 29.3 batch with a temporary vault (`sp-org--write-note` stubbed). Not run on the real `~/notes` or with vulpea.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiAXf5syXqG5HjUbdK7)_",
